cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SourceGuard, the Differential Source Variants (DSV) technique,
  or any part of this repository, please cite it as below and credit
  95LAB.
type: software
title: "SourceGuard: Differential Source Variants for Build Confidentiality under Compiler Compromise"
abstract: >-
  SourceGuard is a build architecture that keeps source code confidential
  even when the compiler is compromised. Each isolated build cell compiles
  a textually different but semantically equivalent source variant; an
  honest compiler yields bit-identical artifacts, so any compiler that
  embeds variant-dependent information causes divergence and is blocked
  by a trusted artifact gateway.
